# CODEOWNERS — one lane owns each path (SOLUSDEV-222 / CTR-07)
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#   Worktrees isolate the filesystem; they do not stop two lanes editing the same
#   file and colliding at merge. Directory ownership, written down, is what does.
#   See docs/WORKTREES.md for the protocol and the lane -> branch mapping.
#
# HOW IT IS ENFORCED
#   GitLab CODEOWNERS is a PREMIUM feature. On Free this file is inert — it does
#   not gate approvals. The real enforcement is the `lint:lane-ownership` CI job
#   (scripts/check-lane-ownership.mjs), which PARSES THIS FILE as its single
#   source of truth. Keep the two in sync by only ever editing this file.
#
# HOW TO READ IT
#   Later rules win (GitLab/GitHub semantics). The `*` default assigns every
#   otherwise-unclaimed path to @shared, so there is no unowned path by
#   construction; a lane line below then claims its subtree. Where a single file
#   inside one lane's directory belongs to another lane, it appears as a
#   more-specific line AFTER that lane's directory line — the two `@lane-systems`
#   entries under `agent/` are the only such cases, and they are called out.
#
# @shared PATHS ARE NOT A FREE-FOR-ALL
#   A lane MR touching an @shared path FAILS the CI check. That is the point:
#   the cross-lane need becomes a LANE 0 contract ticket, not a direct edit
#   (docs/WORKTREES.md "Changing a contract after lanes start"). A human can set
#   the CI variable LANE_OWNERSHIP_OVERRIDE=1 for a one-off; agents never do.
#
# THE LANE HANDLES ARE NOT GITLAB USERS. They are lane identifiers, matched to
# branch names: @lane-<slug> <-> branch SOLUSDEV-<epic#>-lane-<slug>. If GitLab
# Premium is enabled later, create groups with these names.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Default: everything not claimed by a lane below.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*                                                       @shared

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LANE 0 — Platform Contracts & Shared Foundations (SOLUSDEV-36)
# branch: SOLUSDEV-36-lane-contracts
# Listed explicitly rather than left to the `*` default: these are the paths
# LANE 0 writes, and naming them keeps "who owns the contracts" answerable.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/CODEOWNERS                                             @shared
/packages/shared-types/                                 @shared
/packages/api/src/solus_api/contracts/                  @shared
/docs/contracts/                                        @shared
/docs/WORKTREES.md                                      @shared
/scripts/                                               @shared

